menu "Application (headset)"

    config HEADSET_ENABLE_USB
        bool "Enter USOUND at boot (starts the USB device stack)"
        default n
        help
            On the ESP32-S3 the USB-OTG PHY and the built-in USB-Serial/JTAG share
            D+/D-. Starting TinyUSB removes the USJ console until the board is
            re-plugged — and because this image re-takes the PHY about a second
            after every boot, replugging alone does not bring COM4 back: recovery
            is holding BOOT while replugging to reach ROM download mode.

            This is the whole point of the usound profile, so it must eventually be
            y. Leave it n while developing over USJ, and turn it on only with
            someone at the board or once TBD-009 (the UART console bridge) closes.

    config HEADSET_ENABLE_WIRELESS
        bool "Compile the wireless (wlink) profile and enter it when USB is not in use"
        default y
        help
            The Phase 2 profile: duplex audio to the dongle over subsys/audio_link
            (BLE 2M PHY + Opus, ADR-022). Unlike usound it leaves the
            USB-Serial/JTAG console alone, so an image with only this enabled is
            safe to flash remotely. Needs CONFIG_BT_ENABLED.

            With both profiles compiled, USB wins at boot and a long press of the
            action button switches between them. On a board with a battery, USB
            "available" means the charger reports external power.

    config HEADSET_WIRELESS_RETRY_S
        int "Re-enter WIRELESS from IDLE after (s)"
        default 30
        range 5 3600
        depends on HEADSET_ENABLE_WIRELESS
        help
            After the dongle has been gone longer than the profile's reconnect
            grace period the headset drops to IDLE, which releases the radio and the
            stream lock so the device may sleep. It advertises again after this
            long, or at once on a press of the action button.

    # Pins are no longer here: they belong to the board (ADR-025). The devkit's old
    # HEADSET_*_PIN_* settings are BOARD_DEVKIT_* in boards/esp32s3_devkitc/board/Kconfig;
    # ORGA v1's are fixed by its copper in boards/orga_v1/board/board.c.

endmenu
